WEBVTT

00:00:34.201 --> 00:00:36.161
Ah, beer.

00:00:36.345 --> 00:00:39.723
So many choices
and it makes so little difference.

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:41.892
How about Löbrau? It has dots on it.

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:46.480
Overruled! The choice of champions
is Pabst Blue Robot.

00:00:46.563 --> 00:00:49.566
I can't drink that. The metal shavings
make my throat bloody.

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:53.028
Wah, wah, baby wants a Zima.

00:00:53.111 --> 00:00:56.114
Hey, hey, hey, we can all fight
when we're drunk.

00:00:56.198 --> 00:00:58.367
Now, listen, why don't we just
brew our own beer?

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:00.118
You can brew your own beer?

00:01:00.202 --> 00:01:03.497
Sure, the kids at the Orphanarium
used to do it all the time.

00:01:09.044 --> 00:01:10.837
Cursed bacteria of Liberia!

00:01:10.921 --> 00:01:13.715
My own son,
suspended from boarding school.

00:01:13.799 --> 00:01:14.883
It's not my fault, Dad.

00:01:14.967 --> 00:01:16.176
And you, Cubert!

00:01:16.259 --> 00:01:18.178
I cloned you from one of my warts

00:01:18.261 --> 00:01:20.681
and I can send you straight back in there!

00:01:20.764 --> 00:01:22.891
- Nuh-uh!
- What's going on?

00:01:22.975 --> 00:01:25.644
Is this angry yelling
or busted-hearing-aid yelling?

00:01:25.727 --> 00:01:27.729
- I'm afraid it's both.
- What?

00:01:27.813 --> 00:01:30.065
Now, hold on.
Everyone cool your daiquiris.

00:01:30.148 --> 00:01:33.360
Let's give the little vermin
a chance to explain themselves.

00:01:33.443 --> 00:01:35.070
It was self-defense, Mom.

00:01:35.153 --> 00:01:37.823
Just look at this letter
the principal sent.

00:01:40.309 --> 00:01:43.103
We were in science class
and we had just finished building

00:01:43.187 --> 00:01:44.479
a miniature black hole.

00:01:44.563 --> 00:01:46.148
That was easy.

00:01:46.273 --> 00:01:49.401
Pretty scrawny black hole.
It must be hungry.

00:01:50.694 --> 00:01:52.321
Black holes don't need food.

00:01:52.404 --> 00:01:53.947
Neither do nerds!

00:01:57.784 --> 00:01:59.161
My Manwich!

00:02:01.205 --> 00:02:03.290
That's it, Brett.
You've compressed our lunches

00:02:03.373 --> 00:02:05.792
to a singularity for the last time!

00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:07.544
Salt him, Dwight!

00:02:11.381 --> 00:02:15.010
When I re-solidify, I'm going
to put you in a world of goop.

00:02:16.637 --> 00:02:18.388
See? That bully started it.

00:02:18.472 --> 00:02:21.725
We couldn't fight back with brawn,
so we used our brains.

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:24.144
I warned you not to use those things!

00:02:26.647 --> 00:02:29.816
Let's see, we've got our malt, our hops...

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:32.486
We just need a big,
disposable tub to mix it in.

00:02:32.569 --> 00:02:33.570
Yo.

00:02:37.574 --> 00:02:39.910
Now it needs to boil for a couple hours.

00:02:46.667 --> 00:02:48.502
Dwight, you remember the crew.

00:02:48.585 --> 00:02:50.212
Crew, you remember Cubert?

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:54.258
Wonderful! Then I'm sure you won't mind

00:02:54.341 --> 00:02:56.552
being their legal guardians for a month.

00:02:59.096 --> 00:03:00.514
Well, well...

00:03:00.597 --> 00:03:03.350
If it isn't my old friends Stretch-Pants,

00:03:03.433 --> 00:03:04.893
No-Pants and...

00:03:05.769 --> 00:03:06.770
Idiot.

00:03:06.854 --> 00:03:09.064
We're making beer. I'm the brewery.

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:10.816
I heard alcohol makes you stupid.

00:03:10.941 --> 00:03:12.484
No, I'm... Doesn't.

00:03:12.568 --> 00:03:14.862
Actually, Dwight, you're right.

00:03:14.945 --> 00:03:17.489
Alcohol is very, very bad.

00:03:17.573 --> 00:03:18.782
For children.

00:03:18.866 --> 00:03:21.952
But once you turn 21,
it becomes very, very good.

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:23.245
So scram!

00:03:23.328 --> 00:03:25.289
Oh, man, I'm sick of this.

00:03:26.665 --> 00:03:27.875
Hey, Dad.

00:03:27.958 --> 00:03:30.961
What useless contraption
are you half-baking today?

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:32.212
Wuh?

00:03:32.296 --> 00:03:34.631
Oh, this is my latest invention.

00:03:34.715 --> 00:03:38.760
A device that lets anyone
sound exactly like me.

00:03:38.844 --> 00:03:42.014
Good news, everyone! I'm a horse's butt.

00:03:42.097 --> 00:03:45.058
I am? That's not good news
at all, you little...

00:03:46.310 --> 00:03:47.895
What's this device's marketability?

00:03:47.978 --> 00:03:49.438
Who's the target consumer?

00:03:49.521 --> 00:03:52.900
There is no target consumer, only targets.

00:03:53.025 --> 00:03:57.613
Targets that will tremble in fear
as their new masters hand down edicts

00:03:57.696 --> 00:04:00.032
in my glorious booming voice!

00:04:00.282 --> 00:04:02.159
Now, quit pestering me,

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:04.203
you confounded scoundrels!

00:04:04.328 --> 00:04:07.164
Stamp it, file it, oh, yeah

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:09.166
Send it overnight...

00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:10.709
Can I collate that?

00:04:10.792 --> 00:04:12.669
- No.
- Can I shred these contracts?

00:04:12.753 --> 00:04:14.046
No!

00:04:14.713 --> 00:04:16.757
Wow! A power stamper!

00:04:22.179 --> 00:04:23.889
Now look at all the work I got to do!

00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:27.267
Ow!

00:04:34.691 --> 00:04:36.360
Mm. The ingredients are cooked

00:04:36.443 --> 00:04:39.321
and they've picked up some of
your natural robot flavorings.

00:04:39.404 --> 00:04:40.739
Time to add the yeast.

00:04:41.865 --> 00:04:45.994
Yeast? You mean... I'll have
a life-form growing inside me?

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:48.330
It's so beautiful.

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:53.544
Talk to me.

00:04:53.627 --> 00:04:55.671
This is Professor Farnsworth.

00:04:55.754 --> 00:04:58.966
I have an important delivery
for you and your dumb crew.

00:04:59.049 --> 00:05:02.177
You must deliver a pizza to Dogdoo Eight,

00:05:02.261 --> 00:05:04.721
a planet at the edge of the universe.

00:05:04.805 --> 00:05:07.182
Sorry I can't come down to say goodbye

00:05:07.266 --> 00:05:09.810
but I'm busy inventing useless junk.

00:05:09.893 --> 00:05:11.645
And I smell bad.

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:32.124
Hey!

00:05:32.207 --> 00:05:35.377
If you were my kids,
you'd get quite a talking to.

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:36.879
From your father.

00:05:36.962 --> 00:05:38.630
When he got home from the Senate.

00:05:38.714 --> 00:05:41.133
Oh, bother! What have they done now?

00:05:41.216 --> 00:05:44.344
Those pork dumplings
sent us on a fake pizza delivery!

00:05:44.428 --> 00:05:46.013
The address was on Dogdoo Eight,

00:05:46.096 --> 00:05:48.473
but the universe ends
right after Dogdoo Seven.

00:05:48.557 --> 00:05:50.184
Child-mon, is this true?

00:05:50.267 --> 00:05:52.269
Yeah, but why are you mad at us?

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:56.064
Your dummy brigade wasted a week
on an obviously fake mission.

00:05:56.148 --> 00:05:59.526
Plus, they're making bootleg beer
inside company property.

00:05:59.651 --> 00:06:01.653
Lies! Lies and slander!

00:06:03.238 --> 00:06:05.991
Accusing gentle Bender of a misdeed?

00:06:06.074 --> 00:06:07.659
That's the last straw!

00:06:07.743 --> 00:06:09.870
You boys have been underfoot long enough!

00:06:09.953 --> 00:06:12.164
You jerked the words
right out of my mouth.

00:06:12.247 --> 00:06:15.375
We're their fathers,
and it's high times we acted like it.

00:06:15.459 --> 00:06:17.377
Ooh-hoo-hoo, here comes violence.

00:06:19.046 --> 00:06:20.756
Get a job, you lazy kids.

00:06:22.716 --> 00:06:25.427
Uh, I guess if you want children beaten,

00:06:25.511 --> 00:06:27.054
you have to do it yourself.

00:06:30.057 --> 00:06:32.267
Come on, Dad, shuffle faster!

00:06:32.351 --> 00:06:34.603
You don't want to miss the unveiling
of our new company, do you?

00:06:34.686 --> 00:06:35.687
Company?

00:06:37.272 --> 00:06:38.482
How cute.

00:06:38.565 --> 00:06:40.067
What will you be peddling?

00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:42.277
Lemonade? Shoe shines?

00:06:42.361 --> 00:06:43.529
Cootie insurance?

00:06:43.612 --> 00:06:46.532
Perhaps they've constructed
a teddy bear hospital.

00:06:48.492 --> 00:06:51.745
Actually, we're starting
a competing delivery company.

00:06:56.834 --> 00:06:59.211
Welcome to the world of business.

00:07:08.492 --> 00:07:10.911
Hey, who's going to use a delivery service

00:07:11.014 --> 00:07:12.599
with a kicked sign?

00:07:12.733 --> 00:07:14.151
Nobody, that's who!

00:07:14.234 --> 00:07:16.028
But we already have a client signed up.

00:07:16.111 --> 00:07:18.447
We're delivering the Daily Supernova.

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:23.535
So your delivery company
is just a cute, harmless paper route.

00:07:23.619 --> 00:07:24.661
Whew!

00:07:24.745 --> 00:07:26.955
No. It's a serious business.

00:07:27.039 --> 00:07:30.584
Yes, it's a tremendous responsibility,
all right.

00:07:32.377 --> 00:07:34.713
What if a paper were to land in a puddle?

00:07:34.796 --> 00:07:37.466
Civilization as we know it
might get splashed.

00:07:49.728 --> 00:07:52.147
Why do they always treat us
like dumb kids?

00:07:52.231 --> 00:07:55.359
We're practically old enough to
find the Fox Network infantile.

00:07:55.442 --> 00:07:56.610
Yeah, we'll show them.

00:07:56.693 --> 00:08:00.906
All Awesome Express needs
is a sturdy interstellar delivery craft.

00:08:00.989 --> 00:08:02.241
Voilà!

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:04.534
You got a quarter?

00:08:11.833 --> 00:08:15.254
Man, the ad said to allow
four to six seconds for delivery.

00:08:15.337 --> 00:08:17.506
More like seven.

00:08:19.716 --> 00:08:22.344
I'm really starting to swell up with beer.

00:08:22.427 --> 00:08:24.054
I must look ridiculous.

00:08:24.137 --> 00:08:26.181
No. You have a healthy glow.

00:08:26.265 --> 00:08:29.101
Oh, my God!
I just felt it ferment!

00:08:29.184 --> 00:08:30.936
Ooh! Let me feel.

00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:33.188
Have you thought about what to name it?

00:08:33.355 --> 00:08:36.358
I was thinking Benderbrau
if it's an ale...

00:08:36.441 --> 00:08:38.151
Botweiser if it's a lager.

00:08:38.235 --> 00:08:40.362
I hope it's a lager,
so I can take it to a ball game.

00:08:41.697 --> 00:08:44.157
Ooh! I felt that one!

00:08:49.162 --> 00:08:51.498
Oh, there's a crack in the hull here.

00:08:51.582 --> 00:08:54.167
That could cause explosive decompression.

00:08:54.251 --> 00:08:55.502
Put a sticker on it.

00:08:58.922 --> 00:09:01.174
Off on your first delivery, eh?

00:09:01.258 --> 00:09:03.010
You be careful, my little tinkler.

00:09:03.093 --> 00:09:06.138
Remember we used
to call you that, huh? Tinkler?

00:09:08.599 --> 00:09:09.766
Gets moving!

00:09:09.850 --> 00:09:12.561
Those newspapers won'ts
deliver themselveses.

00:09:12.644 --> 00:09:14.813
Only the Sunday edition can do's that.

00:09:16.273 --> 00:09:19.860
Goodness, there must be
50 papers in that bundle.

00:09:19.943 --> 00:09:21.737
That's a big number, 50.

00:09:21.820 --> 00:09:23.238
Yeah, if you're an idiot.

00:09:26.658 --> 00:09:29.077
Three, two, one.

00:09:29.202 --> 00:09:30.537
All systems go.

00:09:30.662 --> 00:09:31.663
Blastoff!

00:09:37.961 --> 00:09:39.254
See you at din-din!

00:09:39.338 --> 00:09:40.797
I'm blowing you a kiss!

00:09:40.881 --> 00:09:42.883
Mwah!

00:09:42.966 --> 00:09:45.344
Aah! Take evasive action!

00:09:45.719 --> 00:09:49.139
It's closing in.
You can't avoid it.

00:09:49.306 --> 00:09:50.933
It's a cheek seeker.

00:09:51.350 --> 00:09:53.560
And... Gotcha!

00:09:53.727 --> 00:09:55.312
No!

00:10:32.057 --> 00:10:33.058
Yeah!

00:10:55.789 --> 00:10:57.666
Business is down, so I have filed papers

00:10:57.749 --> 00:11:00.294
to have you all reclassified as slaves.

00:11:02.212 --> 00:11:06.717
Well, well
if it isn't our little munchkin moguls.

00:11:06.800 --> 00:11:08.844
Would you just...

00:11:08.927 --> 00:11:10.012
What's the trouble, men?

00:11:10.137 --> 00:11:12.264
Need some penny rolls for your profits?

00:11:12.347 --> 00:11:15.434
Actually, thanks to Dwight's
brilliant accounting

00:11:15.517 --> 00:11:18.145
and my unaccountable brilliance...

00:11:18.228 --> 00:11:21.189
...our paper route now has
over a million customers!

00:11:22.482 --> 00:11:24.818
We're finally making more money
than you guys!

00:11:24.902 --> 00:11:26.445
Aren't you impressed now, Pops?

00:11:26.528 --> 00:11:27.779
Aren't you? Aren't you?

00:11:27.863 --> 00:11:30.365
Uh, in a small way, yes.

00:11:30.449 --> 00:11:32.200
But you still don't have your own building

00:11:32.284 --> 00:11:34.036
or conference table or...

00:11:34.119 --> 00:11:35.454
Or one of those things.

00:11:35.871 --> 00:11:36.955
Hello.

00:11:38.749 --> 00:11:41.960
Our dads are never impressed,
no matter what we do.

00:11:42.044 --> 00:11:43.670
Maybe we should start a fire.

00:11:43.754 --> 00:11:47.925
If we really want to impress them,
we'll have to crush them with strategy

00:11:48.008 --> 00:11:49.509
"Dwight Lightning."

00:11:50.886 --> 00:11:54.014
Very well, but I get to
name the next strategy.

00:11:55.933 --> 00:11:58.393
The Sun.

00:11:59.937 --> 00:12:01.480
I'm burning to death!

00:12:01.563 --> 00:12:05.817
Oh! You know how much an apartment
that big would cost on the sun?

00:12:06.652 --> 00:12:09.029
People, as you know, our young sons

00:12:09.154 --> 00:12:12.199
have become great successes
in the very same field as us.

00:12:12.282 --> 00:12:13.951
- That's great!
- All right!

00:12:14.034 --> 00:12:15.994
Naturally, we're humiliated.

00:12:16.078 --> 00:12:18.413
That's why we need you, our loyal crew,

00:12:18.497 --> 00:12:22.125
to make Planet Express
800% more profitable.

00:12:22.209 --> 00:12:24.044
We'll start by slashing salaries

00:12:24.127 --> 00:12:26.046
and this time, I mean really slashing.

00:12:26.129 --> 00:12:28.840
Uh, guys, I don't know how
to tell you this

00:12:28.924 --> 00:12:31.134
so I'll just let Fry
blurt it out thoughtlessly.

00:12:31.218 --> 00:12:32.886
We don't work for you anymore!

00:12:32.970 --> 00:12:33.971
What!

00:12:34.054 --> 00:12:35.556
Dwight and Cubert made us a better offer.

00:12:35.639 --> 00:12:36.765
We're paperboys now.

00:12:36.848 --> 00:12:39.142
Incoming! We got papers to stuff, team.

00:12:39.226 --> 00:12:40.352
Hup to, hup to.

00:12:40.435 --> 00:12:41.520
- Yes, sir.
- Right away.

00:12:41.603 --> 00:12:43.146
We're on it, Mr. Farnsworth.

00:12:49.027 --> 00:12:53.407
Folks, the situation is grim,
but we shall prevail

00:12:53.490 --> 00:12:56.910
thanks to you,
our crack team of loyal dregs.

00:13:00.247 --> 00:13:02.082
I don't even know who this guy is.

00:13:02.207 --> 00:13:03.917
I'm Scruffy, the janitor.

00:13:04.001 --> 00:13:05.544
Yes, of course you are.

00:13:05.627 --> 00:13:08.964
Now, we've got to buckle down
and save Planet Express.

00:13:09.339 --> 00:13:10.757
I'm on break.

00:13:18.557 --> 00:13:21.727
Sorry to interrupt
this whirlwind of activity

00:13:21.810 --> 00:13:23.437
but we have an announcement.

00:13:23.604 --> 00:13:25.314
I direct your attention to these forms

00:13:25.397 --> 00:13:27.733
which I'm presently engaged
in handing to you.

00:13:28.442 --> 00:13:31.737
Sweet guinea pig of Winnipeg,
they've taken over our company.

00:13:31.820 --> 00:13:34.323
Balderdash! I never agreed to that.

00:13:34.406 --> 00:13:38.118
No, but you did declare yourself dead
three years ago as a tax dodge.

00:13:38.201 --> 00:13:39.620
Tax dodge nothing.

00:13:39.703 --> 00:13:41.997
You take one nap in a ditch at the park

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:44.207
and they start declaring you
this and that.

00:13:44.333 --> 00:13:46.752
Either way, I technically
inherit your building

00:13:46.835 --> 00:13:47.878
and your spaceship,

00:13:47.961 --> 00:13:50.172
which means Planet Express is now...

00:13:51.423 --> 00:13:53.091
Awesome Express!

00:13:53.216 --> 00:13:56.094
You rotten kids!

00:13:56.845 --> 00:13:57.930
Uh, will you be hiring?

00:13:58.013 --> 00:14:00.307
- No.
- You rotten kids!

00:14:12.653 --> 00:14:15.447
There, one million papers,
folded and loaded.

00:14:18.325 --> 00:14:21.119
Hey, Leela, help me apply
these flame decals I got in my cereal.

00:14:21.203 --> 00:14:22.746
They'll make the ship go faster.

00:14:22.829 --> 00:14:25.374
And what's your scientific basis
for thinking that?

00:14:25.457 --> 00:14:26.667
I'm 12.

00:14:30.379 --> 00:14:32.339
- Oh...
- Did I ever tell you

00:14:32.422 --> 00:14:34.633
how I used to own that ship?

00:14:40.472 --> 00:14:42.683
There but for the grace of God.

00:14:46.144 --> 00:14:49.481
Hush, little brewski
Don't you leak

00:14:49.565 --> 00:14:52.234
Daddy wants to drink
for at least a week

00:14:53.652 --> 00:14:55.571
Oh, my God! I think it's time!

00:14:55.654 --> 00:14:58.198
Hurry, Leela.
Get some coasters and cold mugs.

00:15:00.784 --> 00:15:02.327
Push, Bender, push.

00:15:04.246 --> 00:15:05.581
You're doing great.

00:15:05.664 --> 00:15:09.543
It feels like I'm trying
to push a waterbed out of me.

00:15:09.626 --> 00:15:12.504
Almost there. Just two more bottles.

00:15:12.588 --> 00:15:13.880
Is it okay?

00:15:13.964 --> 00:15:15.716
I can't hear anything.

00:15:17.384 --> 00:15:20.304
It's an ale! Five gallons, six ounces.

00:15:26.643 --> 00:15:27.895
Hey, what's going on?

00:15:27.978 --> 00:15:30.772
This is a delivery company,
not a delivery room.

00:15:30.856 --> 00:15:33.650
We just busted our buns
delivering a million papers

00:15:33.734 --> 00:15:35.319
and this is how you greet us?

00:15:35.402 --> 00:15:37.571
With a bunch of frosty cold beers?

00:15:37.654 --> 00:15:39.072
Hey, wait a second.

00:15:39.156 --> 00:15:41.867
How did you deliver
a million papers in one hour?

00:15:42.075 --> 00:15:44.411
Uh... We just did, okay?

00:15:44.494 --> 00:15:45.495
'Cause we're awesome.

00:15:45.579 --> 00:15:46.705
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:15:46.788 --> 00:15:47.831
- Awesome.
- Awesome.

00:15:49.207 --> 00:15:52.419
Hello, Awesome Express,
the rude, crude delivery dudes.

00:15:52.502 --> 00:15:53.795
How may I direct your call?

00:15:54.421 --> 00:15:55.464
What's that?

00:15:55.547 --> 00:15:56.924
You haven't gotten your paper?

00:15:57.466 --> 00:15:58.842
In how long?

00:16:07.226 --> 00:16:12.272
Might a homeless old man have
a touch more beef bourguignon?

00:16:12.356 --> 00:16:14.608
And another tequila slammer?

00:16:14.691 --> 00:16:16.568
- Ugh!
- Please?

00:16:16.652 --> 00:16:19.905
Don't you sweet-talk me,
you wrinkly old tube sock.

00:16:20.030 --> 00:16:22.449
May I have one, too, wife?

00:16:22.532 --> 00:16:25.869
You're both pathetic,
being jealous of your own offspring.

00:16:25.953 --> 00:16:28.622
Now, you should be happy
that they became successes

00:16:28.705 --> 00:16:30.958
instead of following in your footsteps.

00:16:31.041 --> 00:16:34.628
Oh, it's true, but they grow up so fast.

00:16:34.711 --> 00:16:37.589
We just wanted a few more years
of being better than them.

00:16:37.673 --> 00:16:39.633
They're so stinking talented

00:16:39.716 --> 00:16:42.803
they don't even need
their fathers anymore.

00:16:48.183 --> 00:16:49.268
Dad!

00:16:49.351 --> 00:16:50.727
We screwed up!

00:16:50.811 --> 00:16:52.771
You did? Tough luck, suckers.

00:16:52.854 --> 00:16:54.439
Please, help us, Pops.

00:16:54.523 --> 00:16:57.484
We agreed to deliver way more
papers than we could handle.

00:16:57.568 --> 00:17:00.320
But we couldn't handle 'em,
so we started dumping the extras

00:17:00.404 --> 00:17:01.738
in a crater on the moon.

00:17:01.822 --> 00:17:04.533
And now everybody's yelling at us
about their missing papers.

00:17:04.616 --> 00:17:06.535
And we don't know what to do.

00:17:12.207 --> 00:17:13.667
- Oh...
- Oh...

00:17:13.750 --> 00:17:16.295
Why did you boys do all this?

00:17:16.503 --> 00:17:19.715
We just wanted you
to be proud of us.

00:17:19.798 --> 00:17:21.091
Proud of you?

00:17:21.174 --> 00:17:23.760
You ruined us
with sleazy business practices

00:17:23.844 --> 00:17:26.221
and a complete disregard
for human decency.

00:17:26.722 --> 00:17:28.432
Of course we're proud of you.

00:17:28.515 --> 00:17:29.892
Damn right we are.

00:17:29.975 --> 00:17:34.187
Now, come on. Let's go do
a little father-son weaseling out of this.

00:17:39.818 --> 00:17:41.904
Good thing
I had this net installed

00:17:41.987 --> 00:17:43.280
for catching giraffes.

00:18:01.757 --> 00:18:05.344
Okay, boys, let me show you
how a paper man does it.

00:18:13.477 --> 00:18:15.687
Au revoir!

00:18:18.148 --> 00:18:19.608
Can I use the gun, Dad?

00:18:19.691 --> 00:18:22.653
Oh, what kind of father
would I be if I said no?

00:18:28.075 --> 00:18:29.618
Only one house to go.

00:18:29.701 --> 00:18:30.702
We did it!

00:18:32.496 --> 00:18:33.538
Yeah!

00:18:38.252 --> 00:18:40.712
Run away.
That bully Brett Blob lives there.

00:18:40.796 --> 00:18:43.173
He's ugly, mean, stupid, stink mucus,

00:18:43.257 --> 00:18:47.219
and last week we sort of broke his window.

00:18:47.678 --> 00:18:49.054
All right, all right.

00:18:49.137 --> 00:18:51.431
What do we do
when we break somebody's window?

00:18:51.515 --> 00:18:52.641
Pay for it?

00:18:52.724 --> 00:18:54.268
Oh, heavens, no.

00:18:54.351 --> 00:18:57.104
We apologize. With nice, cheap words.

00:18:59.982 --> 00:19:03.902
I thought I heard the doorbell
but I see it was the dork bell.

00:19:06.697 --> 00:19:08.824
Uh, you made a funny good one, Brett.

00:19:08.907 --> 00:19:12.035
Now, now, no need to give us the business.

00:19:12.119 --> 00:19:14.121
We'd like a word with your daddy.

00:19:14.204 --> 00:19:16.665
Whatever. Dad!

00:19:16.748 --> 00:19:18.125
Don't worry, boys.

00:19:18.208 --> 00:19:21.295
I'm sure his father
is a perfectly normal, reasonable man.

00:19:21.378 --> 00:19:22.629
What the hell do you want?

00:19:22.713 --> 00:19:25.716
Mr. Blob, our sons have come to apologize

00:19:25.799 --> 00:19:27.551
for damaging your window.

00:19:27.634 --> 00:19:31.263
They've learned their lesson
and they want to make amends.

00:19:31.346 --> 00:19:33.098
- I'm sorry, sir.
- Yeah. Sorry.

00:19:33.181 --> 00:19:34.850
You can shove your apology

00:19:34.933 --> 00:19:37.769
into the bottom of your
one-way digestive system.

00:19:37.853 --> 00:19:38.896
Now, see here!

00:19:38.979 --> 00:19:41.857
We assured our sons
that you'd accept their apology.

00:19:41.940 --> 00:19:43.942
Aw. Tell you what.

00:19:44.318 --> 00:19:48.238
I'll accept their apology
when they kiss my ass!

00:19:48.322 --> 00:19:50.032
Which I don't have!

00:19:52.200 --> 00:19:55.078
No one gives my boy that option.

00:19:55.162 --> 00:19:56.788
Bring it on, Jell-O Pop.

00:19:56.872 --> 00:19:58.874
- Yeah! Get him, Dad!
- Show him who's boss.

00:20:03.378 --> 00:20:04.796
Get him, Pops.

00:20:04.880 --> 00:20:06.006
Hooray?

00:20:19.228 --> 00:20:20.812
That was incredible!

00:20:20.896 --> 00:20:23.899
You are the bravest dads
in the entire trauma center.

00:20:23.982 --> 00:20:26.193
You guys almost had him,
until he digested you.

00:20:26.276 --> 00:20:28.320
Aw, you're good kids.

00:20:29.655 --> 00:20:32.908
If I could feel anything right now,
it would be pride.

00:20:34.993 --> 00:20:37.579
I was wrong! I can still feel pain!

00:20:39.957 --> 00:20:42.000
He's come to finish the job.

00:20:42.084 --> 00:20:44.086
Someone toss me out the window!

00:20:44.169 --> 00:20:45.629
No, no. Wait.

00:20:45.712 --> 00:20:48.715
I... I feel terrible about what happened.

00:20:48.799 --> 00:20:51.301
I've just been under
a lot of stress lately

00:20:51.385 --> 00:20:53.345
down at the plant, you know.

00:20:53.428 --> 00:20:57.474
They're bringing in computers
to "improve productivity,"

00:20:57.558 --> 00:21:00.936
and, well,
that's no excuse for how I acted.

00:21:01.019 --> 00:21:03.897
But the boy needs to see that real men

00:21:03.981 --> 00:21:06.650
solve their disagreements with words,
not violence,

00:21:06.733 --> 00:21:09.653
so, uh, if you'll
accept my apology, well...

00:21:09.736 --> 00:21:12.948
I hope we can put this
embarrassing incident behind us.

00:21:13.365 --> 00:21:15.993
- Mm. I suppose.
- Oh, ah...

00:21:16.535 --> 00:21:17.869
Hey, chumps!

00:21:17.953 --> 00:21:20.080
I heard you were on the ass end
of an ass-kicking,

00:21:20.163 --> 00:21:22.666
so I figured you could use
a couple of these little babies.

00:21:22.749 --> 00:21:23.959
Oh, why not?

00:21:24.042 --> 00:21:26.753
Might as well live it up
as long as I've got this catheter in me.

00:21:26.837 --> 00:21:29.214
Won't you join us, Mr. Blob?

00:21:29.298 --> 00:21:30.674
Sounds like a plan.

00:21:31.842 --> 00:21:34.386
This is what makes life worth clinging to.

00:21:34.469 --> 00:21:37.848
Three fathers enjoying
a day out with their sons.

00:21:38.974 --> 00:21:42.728
It would seem we've taught our boys
a lesson about life.

00:21:42.811 --> 00:21:46.481
Man or blob,
it's what's inside that counts.